35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The data is clear. Projects driven by inspection findings delivered on time. Those based on comfort or appeal slipped significantly.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The timetable records show we paid for off-site space for two terms. Meanwhile, booking data reveals specialist rooms sit idle, while general requests are turned away all year.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The freeze left grounds posts empty, yet technicians have spare hours. Worse, they spend hours on manual checks the old equipment can’t handle.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The diaries show six weeks lost to weather, and comfort projects slip a year. We must prioritize inspection-driven work to protect the calendar.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The plant costs rose a fifth, yet we never reserved funds for the AV kit’s inevitable replacement. We are funding the build, not the lifecycle.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, your point about inspection-driven work is key. The data confirms that only those projects delivered on time. We must anchor our choice in that reality.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I agree. But the booking data shows general rooms are always full, while specialist ones sit empty. We must prioritize high-demand, low-disruption spaces.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Victoria, the demand is real, but the staff to support it is missing. We cannot build more without fixing the staffing gap first.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the staffing gap is real, but the calendar is already broken. We cannot afford another year of slippage. We need a project that fits the remaining weeks.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, the staffing gap is real, but the financial leak is worse. We are buying equipment we cannot afford to replace.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the financial leak is critical, but we must also ask if the space is actually used. My data shows single-wing projects disappoint users.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
